{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments ["<b>And you grow old.</b> He hinted to them that they would be exiled from it at the end of 852 years — the numerical value of ״וְנוֹשַׁנְתֶּם״. And He hastened and exiled them at the end of 850, and hastened it by two years for ״וְנוֹשַׁנְתֶּם״, so that ״כִּי אָבֹד תֹּאבֵדוּן״ would not be fulfilled upon them. And this is what is said (Daniel 9): ״וַיִּשְׁקֹד עַל הָרָעָה וַיְבִיאֶהָ עָלֵינוּ כִּי צַדִּיק ה׳ אֱלֹהֵינוּ״ — He did a kindness with us, that He hastened to bring it two years before its time (Sanhedrin 38; Gittin 8)."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:46:00.573206918Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}